# 1v1, cloud near-misses to the PC (BENCH-253), round 26. Round 25 ran as PR #1036 (BulletCatcher mv and Parallax rp held,
# banked in #1037; Lindada hf did not).
# Round 26 carries three per-robot movement lines that read positive against BOTH controls on the cloud but whose 95%
# low end did not clear 0 there (Robocode 1.12.0, live turn time, c a master copy, aa its A/A twin):
#   ags.Midboss 1q.fast           fq (MOVE-32 flattener views)  +2.48 +- 2.56 vs c / +2.23 +- 2.12 vs aa (24 seeds 92050)
#   demetrix.ForceMajeure 0.75    fq (MOVE-32 flattener views)  +1.29 +- 3.85 vs c / +2.38 +- 1.98 vs aa (12 seeds 94400)
#   cb.mega.RandomBot 1.0         vj (MOVE-44 velocity jitter)  +2.0 +- 3.4 vs c / +3.8 +- 3.1 vs aa (12 seeds 93020)
# This is a confirm with twice the seeds, not a carried cloud lock: the PC reads 24 fresh seeds (half the cloud's
# interval width), and a line ships only on the PC's own read. Expected false passes over 3 robots at the 95% bar: ~0.1.
# Fifteen robots whose lines are already on master (Maui, MadHatter, RammingC, AutoBot, Impact, NanoDeath, Kowari,
# Bicephal, GhostShell, Gridd, Polar, Dreadnaught, Nicator, MoggFanatic, BlackIce) are read only in c and aa, so the A/A
# check reads 18 robots.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       panel-locks.txt  c / aa / fq / vj, 24 fresh seeds from 98300, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks26
#              (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks25)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own lever arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95%
#              low end is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0).
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 25 left this plan's queue state marked complete; the new work directory and seeds mean no
#   battle is read back from an earlier round (and BENCH-272 refights any whose jar changed).
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 936 lock battles (18 robots in c and aa, 3 on a
# lever arm, 24 seeds), about 55 minutes with the live-match check. The prep step stops if any panel robot's jar is missing.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: each line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis, from the top-250 gap diagnosis against BeepBoop 2.0 (truth logs, dzlane/G t50-diag.md, dzlane/L
#     t200-diag.md): all three are MOVE-group robots, where BeepBoop takes fewer hits from the same gun at the same range,
#     so the loss is our movement being learned, not our gun or shield. The flattener views (fq) and velocity jitter (vj)
#     are the two existing movement switches aimed at that: they make our path harder to learn, at a small cost against
#     simple guns. On these three the switch read positive against both controls in every cloud read (screen and lock),
#     where the other 11 MOVE leads of the day each read negative against at least one control in their lock.
#   - The cloud's 12-seed interval (+-2 to +-4 points) is wider than the gain; 24 PC seeds is the cheapest way to settle
#     them, and the gate keeps only what holds on the PC.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa; this lock reads 18, but
# the gate reads aa (multiarm.py prints aa against c), so no aa stop rule is set. The lock halts on 30 failed battles, an
# arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24 or no battle in 30 minutes. The live-match step
# stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines in a PR after this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.24
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks26
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in fq vj; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && for j in $(grep -v "^#" panel-locks.txt | cut -d"|" -f3); do test -f opponents/$j || { echo "missing jar $j"; exit 1; }; done && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks26-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 24 --seed-base 98300 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks26-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks26-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks26-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms fq vj --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks26-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks26-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks26-results "1v1 cloud near-misses, round 26 (Midboss fq, ForceMajeure fq, RandomBot vj) on 24 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks26-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks26-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks26-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks26-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
